right: The first if runs (4 > 3) and makes x 2. The second if is checked afterwards, with x = 2: `2 > 3` is False, so its else runs and x becomes 12.
wrong: Follow x line by line. 4 > 3 → x = 4 - 2 = 2. Then the second if checks the new value: 2 > 3 is False → else → x = 2 + 10 = 12.
